  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "4 LLM agents + 1 rule-based service",
      "items": [
        "One LangGraph runtime — Intake Tracker is rule-based, not LLM",
        "Persona on each box, guardrail on hover. Full detail: agent-specifications.md",
        "Color key matches lfi-pipeline-v1's automation-role legend (teal=LLM-only, peach=LLM+tool, gold=deterministic); security/gold-adjacent here also covers platform infra (LLM Inference, Secrets Manager, Observability, Tracing & Eval) that isn't itself an agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Threat model (ADR-0019)",
      "items": [
        "LLM Inference Service isolated in its own security zone — only the 4 LLM agents may call it, over mTLS",
        "Secrets Manager holds SFTP/DB/mTLS creds; Fraud DB encrypted at rest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "HITL checkpoints (ADR-0016)",
      "items": [
        "HITL checkpoints with SLAs — full current table in agent-specifications.md; count not restated here since it grows as new checkpoints are added (fixes Principal Engineer audit 4.3, which found this card stale after ADR-0029)",
        "Primary trust metric: human-agreement rate. Near-100% = automation-bias risk, not a win"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Observability & evaluation (ADR-0016)",
      "items": [
        "OTel + Prometheus/Grafana for infra; self-hosted Langfuse traces every LLM call and hosts evals",
        "Citation-validity rate gates CI before any prompt/model change ships"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Deployment (ADR-0013/0014/0015)",
      "items": [
        "On-prem for now; LLM self-hosted, Qwen Coder / gpt-oss-120b as swappable candidates",
        "Identity via CBUAE SSO; Fraud DB is Oracle, isolated subnet"
